Z||000000||moonie||08-27-2000||11:14 AM||||i need to buy a 4 cyl head.<BR>how much should i expect to pay for it at a local junkyard ?<BR>also , is there anything i need to look out for ? <BR>last question...does it HAVE to be off a fiero or any 85 pontiac 4 cyl ?<P>i took my head to be ground & it was too cracked up to fix  or to be of any good . the guy at the shop said he could order me another head for $250.00 .  since i'm kinda strapped for cash , i'm hoping one from a junkyard will be a lot cheaper.<P>thanks, <BR>Moonie<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||08-27-2000||11:40 AM||||The head does not have to be from a fiero. I think any head from an 86 and down will fit any 2.5 86 and down. Any head 87 and up will fit any 2.5 87 and up. The Junkyard has a special book called a Hollander manual that tells them what year and make 2.5 head will fit your car. You would be better off though getting a reconditioned head like the ones from the fiero store because any head from a junkyard is probably not going to be much better than the head you have.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.leaderind.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.leaderind.com/</A> <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||rprevo||08-27-2000||07:54 PM|||| You have to be carefull with the different<BR>2.5 heads, Some are open chamber and some<BR>are closed chamber, it will effect the <BR>performance and it might screw with piston<BR>Clearence. I know this for a fact cause I had<BR>an 84 Iron Duke out of a Olds Cutlass ciera<BR>and my chamber in the head was shaped like<BR>a heart thats considered closed chamber<BR>if its shaped like a circle it's<BR>considered a open chamber,<P> Ray<BR>||||reg||1
